# Minimum Project Glossary

Every project maintains a glossary of domain terms. This ensures ubiquitous language across engineering, business, and AI agents.

The glossary defines:

- Business terms and their precise definitions
- Enums and their possible values
- Acronyms and abbreviations used in code

Code that uses a domain term must use **exactly** the same name as the glossary — no translations, ad-hoc abbreviations, or creative synonyms.

When introducing a new domain term, add it to the glossary before using it in code.
